      "id": "frag-6",
      "focal_uid": 6,
      "title": "Rivals cap the price",
      "insight": "Competing accelerators \u2014 AMD's Instinct line and cloud providers' own chips \u2014 set how much Nvidia can charge for a B200-hour. AI demand and the looming next generation both push on it, and it feeds straight into the price and the second-hand market. When competition heats up, the B200 loses pricing power.",
